section promissory appendix is:

section type definitions is:

section useful functions is:

the lesser of a number N with a number M is a value if
    N > M
    and the value is equal to M
    otherwise the value is equal to N.

the greater of a number N with a number M is a value if
    N > M
    and the value is equal to N
    otherwise the value is equal to M.

the base to the power of a base B with an exp E is a number M if
    0 is equal to E
    and M is equal to 1
    otherwise 0 is equal to B
    and E < 0
        and the na n is M
        otherwise M is equal to 0
    otherwise 1 is equal to E
    and M is equal to B
    otherwise E > 0
    and an exp K = E - 1
    and the base to the power of B with K is a number P
    and M = B * P
    otherwise an exp Q = 0 - E
    and the base to the power of B with Q is a number R
    and M = 1 / R.

a money is money at least equal within error for a second money if
    the currency of the money is a text
    and the text is equal to the currency of the second money
    and the value of the second money is a number N
    and the value of the money >= N - 0.05.

